Package: plank
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
	libplank1 (= ${binary:Version}),
	libplank-common (= ${binary:Version}),
	bamfdaemon
Recommends: plank-docklets (= ${binary:Version})
Replaces: plank-docklets (<< 0.12-1)
Description: stupidly simple dock
 Plank is meant to be the simplest dock on the planet. The goal is to provide
 just what a dock needs and absolutely nothing more.
 .
 This package provides the plank executable, its session data and the
 application/menu icons.
 .
 The dock only shows running applications when the org.ayatana.bamf service is
 available on the session bus, which is why bamfdaemon is a hard dependency.

Package: libplank1
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libplank-common (= ${binary:Version})
Description: library for creating dock programs
 Plank is not only a dock, it is also a library that can be extended to create
 other dock programs with more advanced features.
 .
 This package contains the shared library.

Package: plank-docklets
Section: x11
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libplank1 (= ${binary:Version})
Description: docklets for Plank
 Small applets that can be added to a Plank dock: application launcher list,
 clipboard, clock, CPU monitor, desktop switcher, battery and trash.

Package: libplank-common
Section: libs
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: common files for the Plank library and dock
 Dock themes and translations shared by plank and libplank1.

Package: libplank-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, libplank1 (= ${binary:Version}),
	libglib2.0-dev, libgtk-3-dev, libcairo2-dev, libgee-0.8-dev
Description: development files for the Plank library
 Headers, pkg-config file and Vala bindings needed to build docks and docklets
 against libplank.
